{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted","id":1292632,"title":"The atmosphere of Abyssal Exalted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-27T15:47:54-08:00","id":1292632,"title":"The atmosphere of Abyssal Exalted","content":"For those of you who are fans of the Abyssal Exalted...why? What kinds of stories can you tell with them that you couldn't otherwise? What's necromancy like? What are their Charms like? What changes are you looking forward to with 3e Abyssals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T18:06:48-08:00","id":1292660,"title":"","content":"So, this is in the context of a setting hack I'm working up, and not part of the core setting. But, at the heart of it is a desire to remix the basic assumptions of Exalted, which I think might be interesting topic fuel. <br /> <br /> In the setting hack, there are essentially shard realms called Aeons. Sometimes they pass on from Creation, falling away into the Underworld (or forming a pocket Underworld of their own) and becoming, after a fashion, the ghostly remains of an entire kingdom. Or entire religion, empire, continent, stronghold, or any other sort of place or concept that has a definite boundary. <br /> <br /> So, the Abyssals that I'm presenting are on the boundary between the fallen Aeons and Creation. On the one side, the Abyssals and their Deathlord masters are unable to resolve whatever issues led to their Aeon's fall and struggle to restore them. On the other side, Abyssals act as reapers who seek to cut away the fallen Aeons and commit them to Oblivion. <br /> <br /> The stories I have in mind for them are presently more a jumble if ideas yet. But I'm hoping to cover topics like the tragedy of being unable to let go, the temptation to seize ancient power, the return of old rivalries thought passed, and maybe see if I can sneak in a bit of a nostalgia trip for better days buried in Aeons long lost. <br /> <br /> I don't have a specific thought in mind for Charms or Necromancy, but I am specifically keeping them as Solars whose glory is tarnished by association with decay and fall.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T18:57:37-08:00","id":1292675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted#post1292632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those of you who are fans of the Abyssal Exalted...why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, Abyssals have to be the Exalted I'm least sure of why I find anything compelling. I mean, I <b>do</b> feel a draw to them but I don't fully get why. I guess the root from the past might have been primarily on some of the cosmetic details, the general Exaltation story, and... probably a lot of them being associated with ghosts. Ghosts may have often had problem mechanics, but I've always found the concepts and imagery around them to be a big draw.<br /> <br /> Hmmm, also some of the stuff surrounding the dichotomy with the Solars.<br /> <br /> Anything I say should be taken with a grain of salt, because my attempts to actually read stuff from the Abyssals Manual has often been hampered by my issues with finding it engaging, which leaves big gaps in my practical knowledge about them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kinds of stories can you tell with them that you couldn't otherwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that, now and in prior Editions, the most unambiguous answer to that could be stories in which one does emerge to be a scourge of the Age of Sorrows in a manner similar to the Solars, except where unlike them you more generally get to start off embedded in the upper echelons of some grand, gaudy, gothic kingdom beyond the grave.<br /> <br /> I think that there are a bunch of as yet untapped implications of that which I hope the new Edition will capitalise on, but that's the basic core difference. When they ultimately came along, even the Infernals weren't quite like that, considering both how their support network in Creation was more restricted and the general character of Hell is reasonably different than that of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> And stories in which you're actively trying to end the world, which I think has its own appeals.<br /> <br /> Also stuff with relating to the Deathlords; none of the other Exalted entail quite such direct personal associations with their patrons, and stories relating to that melodrama can end up being distinct to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are their Charms like?</div> </div> </div> </div>In prior Editions, still fairly close overall to those of Solars, just with the cosmetics changed. It mixed in some stuff to diminish the strengths or successes of others, some powers for raising zombies and creating and spreading poison and disease, some Charms to get particular boosts of superhuman power from leaning more deeply into experiencing Whispers from the Neverborn, and a Charm to let them acquire and use some Solar Charms.<br /> <br /> They also had the Spectral keyword, which restricted the effectiveness of some of their powers outside of the Underworld and shadowlands, but that was ultimately regarded as not the best idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What changes are you looking forward to with 3e Abyssals?</div> </div> </div> </div>The chivalry of the dead to hopefully give them activity and personality a bit more inclined towards gothic melodrama. Some adjustments to the personas and activities with Deathlords and relationships with their Exalted, both to make them slightly more engaging figures in the setting and expand on interesting possible relationships, and powers that will incorporate a wider variety of macabre, funereal, undead and gothic imagery.<br /> <br /> Hmm, that powers one is vague...<br /> <br /> Charms that draw inspiration in form and function from the imagery of the Deathlords.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T21:19:59-08:00","id":1292699,"title":"","content":"Well, have you watched any of the <i>Mystery Skulls</i> music videos on YouTube?<br /> <br /> Have you ever wanted to play as Dracula, or as <i>Castlevania</i>'s Alucard? Or <i>Hellsing's</i> Alucard.<br /> <br /> One of the characters from <i>Black Rock Shooter</i>, in their Underworld-like Otherworld?<br /> <br /> Spawn?<br /> <br /> The Punisher?<br /> <br /> Celty, from <i>Durararara!</i><br /> <br /> Guts the Black Swordsman from <i>Berserk?</i> (Dammit, that's where they're finally going to publish a greatsword Martial Art, isn't it?)<br /> <br /> <br /> The Abyssal Exalted are going to be a lot more Tim Burton than before. Halloween Town and <i>Corpse Bride</i> and <i>Darkstalkers</i>. Spooky scary skeletons, bizarre ghostly powers and transformations and conjurations.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to them mimicking the miraculous and unhallowed powers of 13+ Deathlords who each embody a different kind of Evil Overlord or vision of the Afterlife. The First and Forsaken Lion is why Abyssal Charms let you be Darth Vader, and some other Deathlord is how you can be <i>The Mummy</i> who rules over a Netherworld of burning sand and endless thirst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T21:38:40-08:00","id":1292702,"title":"","content":"The goth/vampire aesthetic is really hecking cool. Probably more of it than I'd like to think just comes from black being a better colour than gold, and black-robed necromancers at the head of a zombie horde being metal as hell. Aside from that, it's the emotions they focus on. Ambiguous and troubling concepts of morality, internal struggles, tragedy in both the fall of a perhaps good and noble person into a bleak servant of death and in the concept of a tragic cursed hero who can never truly be one of the people they try to protect. It's all stuff you <i>can </i>do with other Exalts, but Abyssals are custom made to do it best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":3559,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","user":"Lanaya","date":". 02-28-2019, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T22:10:03-08:00","id":1292703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1292699#post1292699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Dammit, that's where they're finally going to publish a greatsword Martial Art, isn't it?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, has there ever been a query after something like an Executioner Style?<br /> <br /> That puts me in mind of how Abyssals might be an inroad for more of a dark fantasy style and theme than the other Exalted really have, in terms of their own characterisation, how they take the world, and what they bring into it.<br /> <br /> Heh, that's returning my thoughts to a certain prominent example of somebody who looks like the image of what I think would be very evocative in Abyssal Exalted, that neither Solars nor even Lunars would quite capture in the same way; of the savage and regal Slave Knight Gael.<br /> <br /> Just look at the things he does: his beautiful ruin.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2y2NBCVdyJ4\" data-code=\"2y2NBCVdyJ4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/2y2NBCVdyJ4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T03:48:14-08:00","id":1292725,"title":"","content":"I haven't really been a fan of the Abyssal Exalted, historically speaking... But I would sort of like to be, y'know? There's a lot about them that I find really compelling, but there's also a lot about them that has driven me away.<br /> I like the associations with ghosts, the Underworld and death in general. I love their whole 'brought back from the brink of death' thing, alongside their occasionally-ridiculous elaborate titles and undead aesthetic, though I do believe that the latter can be too uniformly black a lot of the time. I even find their close relationship to their patrons pretty interesting, though I do have a lot of issues with how said relationship (and patrons) have been portrayed in previous editions.<br /> I dislike how-... Limited they've felt historically. They could either be one-note omnicidal villain or a rebellious anti-hero, with few other options. I guess that derives from a particularly 'Oblivion-focused' view of the Deathlords. I'm not a fan of their whole omnicidal-Oblivion thing in general.<br /> <br /> I don't know. It may be that the Abyssal Exalted aren't really for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T05:08:23-08:00","id":1292734,"title":"","content":"Fun fact: I used to find Abyssals perhaps the least compelling of the the exalted. Then a story seed took root in my mind and I realised I could only really do it justice with Abyssal protagonists. I thought the campaign would last maybe a year. That was 2015. <br /> <br /> Now granted, I still don't find the idea of &quot;villain protagonist&quot; Abyssals very interesting (except may as a one-shot when you feel like hamming it up), but there are stories you can tell with heroic Abyssals. It's not that they're stories you <i>can't</i> tell with other exalts, in most cases, but as Lanaya said earlier, Abyssals are particularly well suited to certain themes. <br /> <br /> Abyssals are a new and emerging power in the world and people are uncertain how to react to them, and all the while existing power structures are weakening, giving you a chance to seize this unique moment in history to write your legend across the sky. In blood, probably. You can tell a story of the struggle between your noble ideals and your cursed nature. You can forge your way in a world that rejects your very nature and try to find and maintain personal connections even while most of the world reviles you as a monster. If all of this sounds rather Solaresque, that's kinda my point. Abyssals take all of the &quot;tragic hero&quot; aspects of playing a Solar and dial them up a few notches. So if you really want to lean into those themes as a prospective Solar player, you could do worse than playing an Abyssal instead. <br /> <br /> That and there's all the stories you can tell of exploring the Underworld, but it's getting a major makeover this edition and we're not sure exactly what it's going to look like. Apparently it's less a geographical mirror of Creation with the colour saturation turned way down, and more a series of culturally specific afterlives, so if there isn't some way to play a valkyrie I'd be surprised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T05:40:59-08:00","id":1292743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1292702#post1292702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in the concept of a tragic cursed hero who can never truly be one of the people they try to protect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now now, what is more central and unifying to the human race than the inescapable reality of death?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T07:05:18-08:00","id":1292753,"title":"","content":"I've liked Abyssals since I first saw them---not because I really wanted to revel in being Big Shitty Jim, but because I like the idea of a character still being able to do arguably good or constructive things despite being inherently linked to power that is generally destructive.<br /> Abyssals also have the fun &quot;become very powerful by dying/almost dying&quot; angle, which makes them a shoe-in for revenge angles. The most recent Abyssal I played was/is (unsure if that game is dead or napping) essentially still lashing out at the person (now dead by her hand) who refused to let her follow her desires and tried to kill her for daring to pursue them.<br /> I guess that leads to another point---there's a certain catharsis in playing a character who is not necessarily emotionally healthy on all fronts, and while obviously any Exalt can do that, the Abyssal condition supports it very well.<br /> <br /> Also, spooky ghost stuff is just hella neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T07:21:26-08:00","id":1293289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1292675#post1292675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In prior Editions, still fairly close overall to those of Solars, just with the cosmetics changed. <b>It mixed in some stuff to diminish the strengths or successes of others</b>, some powers for raising zombies and creating and spreading poison and disease, some Charms to get particular boosts of superhuman power from leaning more deeply into experiencing Whispers from the Neverborn, and a Charm to let them acquire and use some Solar Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Never having gotten to really play prior editions of Exalted, this bit was what I heard about and it intrigued me. The image I had in my head was like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karnak_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\">Karnak</a> from the Inhumans, able to see the weaknesses around them and exploit them due to their connection with death and entropy. Like the Euthanatos from Mage: Ascension. And I admit, I like the horror imagery and the desire to turn it around onto the people who (arguably) deserve it the most. I guess what I'm really asking, deep down, is if the Abyssals actually offered that in play, and if there's a good chance they'll offer more of that in this newest edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T08:35:07-08:00","id":1293296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1293289#post1293289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Never having gotten to really play prior editions of Exalted, this bit was what I heard about and it intrigued me. The image I had in my head was like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karnak_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\">Karnak</a> from the Inhumans, able to see the weaknesses around them and exploit them due to their connection with death and entropy. Like the Euthanatos from Mage: Ascension. And I admit, I like the horror imagery and the desire to turn it around onto the people who (arguably) deserve it the most. I guess what I'm really asking, deep down, is if the Abyssals actually offered that in play, and if there's a good chance they'll offer more of that in this newest edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Off the top of my head, the only thing I could refer to of it is literally taking some of the successes from other peoples' dice pools.<br /> <br /> And even then, I'm starting to doubt it... was it not just something in the core book, that they ended up drumming out of the full Manual, and ended up being an Ebon Dragon Charm thing?<br /> <br /> I think some of the suggestions of themes deriving from a few Deathlords might include such an idea, and I think Third Edition's Charm presentation might have more to do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T09:22:44-08:00","id":1293303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1293296#post1293296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even then, I'm starting to doubt it... was it not just something in the core book, that they ended up drumming out of the full Manual, and ended up being an Ebon Dragon Charm thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>They were a major element in their 1st edition design that was almost entirely abandoned by MoEP:Abyssals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T16:45:05-08:00","id":1293368,"title":"","content":"I guess what I'm hoping for is a bit of Karnak, the Euthanatos, and the undead in the form of vampires and liches to be a big part of the theme for the Abyssals this time around. I hope so. that would be something I'd be dying to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T05:01:52-08:00","id":1293449,"title":"","content":"The mention of Karnak highlights something I think that Ex3 is going to do really well.<br /> <br /> 2e had this mythical divergence point where Abyssals were supposed to become almost unrecognisible from the black painted Solars they started out as but were never really given that room to grow. I want to say that the Ink Monkeys Abyssal charms were the closest we had to that but I was involved enough in spitballing ideas for that to feel awkward praising it (aren't I great for suggesting Abyssals should have charms that reduce visibility for having light-consuming black animas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) but alas, I digress.<br /> <br /> Supernal ability and having a charm trees like Awareness not abruptly end at 6 charms facilitates a character whose sense of touch has been honed into a deadly weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T08:10:45-08:00","id":1293473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1292703#post1292703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, has there ever been a query after something like an Executioner Style?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have asked Robert multiple questions surrounding zweihander Martial Arts and Violet Bier of Sorrows Style.<br /> <br /> He seemed to be of the opinion that an Executioner Style would be distinct from whatever the hell Violet Bier of Sorrows Style is supposed to be.<br /> <br /> And what else would a Maiden of Endings Style be if not a style that traditionally uses a two-handed executioner's sword in the spirit of an executioner?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T10:15:18-08:00","id":1293503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1293473#post1293473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what else would a Maiden of Endings Style be if not a style that traditionally uses a two-handed executioner's sword in the spirit of an executioner?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the Sids books, Saturn's associated with a sword, but it's not specified as being any particular type of sword (which's in keeping with the constellation of the Sword, which isn't associated with execution). Per Glories, she's also associated with shears, in the spirit of Atropos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 03-03-2019, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T16:19:54-08:00","id":1293566,"title":"","content":"The Chivalry of the Dead concept has ignited an interest in Abyssals with me for the first time, so I'm quite excited to see where the writers take it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T17:15:31-08:00","id":1293584,"title":"","content":"I started out liking Abyssals b/c Solars had a lot of in-setting historical baggage attached to them that I thought would get stale really quick. Its not that the Solar fluff was bad, its just that Abyssals had this whole new avenue to work down while still being (in fluff but not in crunch) just as powerful. Like, the Solars had Limit Break and that occasionally took away something that's really important for a heroic character to have, self-mastery. Too much limit and a solar turns into a horrible caricature of themselves, but Abyssals stayed in control of themselves, though Resonance ended up being a horrible mechanic. I also liked the Neverborn and how alien they were, Yozis did this too occasionally, but the fact that they were so neurotic made them seem more like over-powerful adult-children than eldritch unknowable god-monsters. But the Neverborn stayed pretty alien throughout the fluff, and the parts of them that were humanized tended to be the parts full of pathos.<br /> <br /> Chivalry of Death seems really interesting, and I really hope the 3e devs do more with the concept of Oblivion, the Neverborn, and the Underworld. Like, maybe being a ghost shouldn't be portrayed as an objectively horrible unnatural tragedy when the alternative is having your identity wholly scoured away Lethe followed by reassignment into an arbitrary reincarnation unless you bribed the right god. This where 1e and 2e failed in that regard b/c IRL reincarnation doctrines tend to have reincarnation depend on your previous life actions(and both of the two most prominent ones portray escape from the cycle as the ultimate goal), whereas Creation seems to just randomly assign reincarnations(despite Immaculate Order propaganda) unless the individual in question worshipped the right god like Ahlat, who would reward their loyalty by turning them into clothing ornaments or something equally servile. But ghosts were always portrayed as being &quot;wrong&quot; for holding onto their identities, engaging in transhumanism, or just wanting to retain some measure of agency(all of which are things I find admirable). Like, even Oblivion warped spectres have this weird Abyss-&quot;enlightenment&quot; whereas Lethe is ultimately a recycling plant intended to churn out blank slate prayer batteries.<br /> <br /> Another thing is that 3e (I hope) seems to be making the Neverborn less overwhelmingly awful with Chivalry of Death. Their existence is one of constant pain and misery, maybe self-righteous contempt shouldn't be the right way to fight them. Though this is probably hoping for too much.<br /> <br /> Also, as evidenced by my username, i've a fondness for fantasy undeath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24948,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","user":"HamSandLich","date":". 03-03-2019, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T17:57:07-08:00","id":1293591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1292703#post1292703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, has there ever been a query after something like an Executioner Style?<br /> <br /> That puts me in mind of how Abyssals might be an inroad for more of a dark fantasy style and theme than the other Exalted really have, in terms of their own characterisation, how they take the world, and what they bring into it.<br /> <br /> Heh, that's returning my thoughts to a certain prominent example of somebody who looks like the image of what I think would be very evocative in Abyssal Exalted, that neither Solars nor even Lunars would quite capture in the same way; of the savage and regal Slave Knight Gael.<br /> <br /> Just look at the things he does: his beautiful ruin.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2y2NBCVdyJ4\" data-code=\"2y2NBCVdyJ4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/2y2NBCVdyJ4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>Dark Souls</i>(and games inspired by it, like <i>Hollow Knight</i>) represent a really interesting take on concepts like &quot;The Abyss&quot; and &quot;Darkness.&quot; Its not that &quot;Dark&quot; is really inherently good therefore &quot;Light&quot; is evil, nor is it vice versa. Its that you can get both helpful and harmful conclusions from the Dark Soul. And even when things associated with the Abyss are being harmful, its still often portrayed as tragic for them, whether they're overwhelmed by emotions they were never taught how to deal with or they've decided to spite a world that automatically rejects them. Sure you've got jerks like Aldrich, but you also have woobies like Gael and Karla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T18:17:15-08:00","id":1293600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1293591#post1293591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Dark Souls</i>(and games inspired by it, like <i>Hollow Knight</i>) represent a really interesting take on concepts like &quot;The Abyss&quot; and &quot;Darkness.&quot; Its not that &quot;Dark&quot; is really inherently good therefore &quot;Light&quot; is evil, nor is it vice versa. Its that you can get both helpful and harmful conclusions from the Dark Soul. And even when things associated with the Abyss are being harmful, its still often portrayed as tragic for them, whether they're overwhelmed by emotions they were never taught how to deal with or they've decided to spite a world that automatically rejects them. Sure you've got jerks like Aldrich, but you also have woobies like Gael and Karla.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about the cosmology of <i>Hollow Knight</i>, but there's a strongly convincing case that the Dark and the Abyss of <i>Dark Souls</i> was only ever so violently dangerous because of the wounds Gwyn inflicted upon it in his futile attempts to contain it.<br /> <br /> Granted, I think the reason Gwyn feared and hated the Dark Soul was because it was the only Lord Soul that grew larger, and the larger it grew, the more power it drained away from the First Flame that birthed it, the weaker the First Flame grew, the weaker the other three Lord Souls became.<br /> <br /> This theft might have been a trick the Furtive Pygmy deliberately wrought, given that he explicitly split the Dark Soul among all of his descendants specifically to encourage its rampant and unchecked growth. Which definitely would have angered Gwyn fiercely, such that even those humans who joined the gods in their war against the dragons were branded as slaves and given no honor for their great valor and achievements.<br /> <br /> The Curse of Undeath was likely a collaborative effort with Nito, the First of the Dead, and possibly also the Witch of Izalith, both of whom would also want to keep from losing their powers. Thus, the Dark Sign is a burning ring of fire that consumes an Undead's humanity when they die, then reviving them as hollow monsters driven to kill other humans to fill themselves with a new piece of the Dark Soul.<br /> <br /> And the Linking of the Fire is a ritual to feed an Undead loaded with much of the Dark Soul back into the First Flame, reducing the Dark Soul's size and returning its stolen power back into the source of all four Lord Souls.<br /> <br /> But the longer time marches on, the larger the Dark Soul becomes, and the more impossible it is for any Undead to gather enough of it to return to the First Flame. Eventually, an Undead (or specifically, an Ashen One) will consume the remains of the First Flame itself, taking all of the power into the Dark Soul, extinguishing the other three Lord Souls, and ushering in the true Age of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Finally free from the curse of undeath, the Dark's more peaceful nature would win out.<br /> <br /> I think Aldric had some sort of &quot;heretical&quot; cult about a future Age of the Deep? Where the Darkness became like abyssal water?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T19:12:14-08:00","id":1293621,"title":"","content":"Its somewhat ambiguous whether or not Dark is dangerous inherently despite being useful(like say, fire). Interestingly, beings of Dark seem to be drawn to the fire they lack. Humans even in the Ringed City were in absolute awe of the gods(who in turn treated them as chattel and vermin), humans linked the fire, even Nashandra from Dark Souls two was obsessed with the First Flame (whether the prospect of snuffing it out or simply possessing power over it as a function of being the personification of Manus's Want). But any power, used incorrectly, can cause harm. It happened with the Witch of Izalith accidentally creating Chaos, it happened with Seath's obsession with immortality. Humans and the Dark Soul got slapped with &quot;designated villain&quot; quite early on by Anor Londo and the association colored nearly every interaction with the Dark from then on.<br /> <br /> As for Hollow Knight, The Void is primordial darkness, equally capable of creation and destruction. Powerful, unknowable, and terrifying, but not actively malicious. Its not actively anything, it just IS and IS NOT. And because of that, you can pull all sorts of things from it: magic, shades that can animate automata, vessels for holding power, etc. At the same time, those qualities make it dangerous for anyone who isn't careful and its power <i>can</i> be abused. This contrasts it with the Pale King(resident Vendrick expy, who is associated with both light and dark) and the final boss(resident Gwyn expy, who is associated with searing hateful solar light):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NUn21rFoFlg&amp;t=229s\" data-code=\"NUn21rFoFlg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/NUn21rFoFlg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T20:24:39-08:00","id":1293646,"title":"","content":"The first thing from Dark Souls that I would draw upon to inform Abyssals would be... the aesthetic. It's a rich aesthetic, that can readily inform things like the Underworld itself, the look and mythology of Abyssals themselves (lot of broken remains of fallen heroes in Dark Souls), and the manner in which they might perceive the world.<br /> <br /> The cosmology, not so much, it's too different. The closest thing would be the vague idea that, while the Dark is scary, there's also a certain comforting serenity to it.<br /> <br /> No, the second thing that I would draw upon would be a thing that pervades the whole series but never actually serves as a direct focus and so also happens to be one of its most ambiguous elements; the nature of undeath itself.<br /> <br /> By which I mean various interpretations of the origin and significance of undeath, and the tension arising from the ambiguity.<br /> <br /> Why are there undead in Dark Souls? Is it because an artificially prolonged Age is basically warping the nature of souls, causing them to cling to living vessels past the point where any meaning or purpose or vitality is retained? Is it a consequence of the Age coming to an end diminishing souls to the point where they're imbalanced and the remaining dark force in them becomes a mindless and insatiable hunger? Is it the true nature and legacy of humanity revealing itself as the power of divinity fades away? Is it just people becoming contaminated by the general wrongness of the world to give them a degenerative condition that is threatening to those around them? Is it just that the person really did kind of die, and something messed up keeps the body going until it forgets all semblance of its life?<br /> <br /> Who knows? Never firmly examined, and different characters in the setting have different opinions about it, not all of whom are entirely forthcoming. The third game introduced the intriguing notion of a religion saying that being not merely undead but actually Hollow (i.e. the final stage where basically all human semblance has disappeared) is actually empowering, and they want a new age in which the cosmological Fire is still around, but the undead have the reins of it.<br /> <br /> In Exalted terms, I wouldn't be thinking about zombies specifically, but I think it's a source of idea and an underlying tension from which various Abyssals could draw.<br /> <br /> So things like a question of whether or not undeath is a superior state to life, or at least will be by the time that you're done with it. Or the process of dying and state of being dead having an aesthetic or philosophical value that is unique to it, and they're going to be the advocates and champions of that.<br /> <br /> In addition to ones of the attitude that the state of the Underworld, or state of Creation for that matter, constituting a perverse attachment to life long after it should be apparent that things have come to a conclusion, and they're the ones empowered to see it through to its end.<br /> <br /> As well as some more death cult-y ones, whether they're in the mould of &quot;life was never all that great, I'd best ease it along&quot; or the more fascistic &quot;life is only truly affirmed by ending in an impressive and meaningful way on your own terms&quot;.<br /> <br /> Plus the more straightforward ones, as champions within and over the world of the dead itself, being well-suited to functioning as heroes and Lawgivers in that environment while having no special concern for extending that power over the living before their time, or ones who see Creation as a dying world, that they see no power to save but also no desire to help along, and that it deserves heroes who won't try to sugarcoat that decay beyond trying to help people find ways to accept and internalize it, as well as opposing the figures trying to give it false hope.<br /> <br /> Right down to the ones who aren't deeply philosophical about their own place or implications, they're just empowered by their own wounds and the magic that flows around that image, and wield it to what ends suit it.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't necessarily view these as villainous, but I would think that most of the more established, conventional powers would, and that can be compounded a bit by attaching a bit of traditionally villainous imagery to the Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T05:53:41-08:00","id":1293716,"title":"","content":"I'd be interested in them making the Void more than &quot;horrible death pit forever.&quot; That's simplistic and has the effect of placing Lethe into &quot;designated right choice&quot; when, again, its really just a recycling plant. The Dowager was pulling all kinds of Abyss linked crap out of the Well of Udr and The Emissary of the Righteous Victory is implied to be a &quot;Saint of the Void&quot; i.e. someone who entered it and came back. In Dark Souls III, the Abyss isn't implied to be emptiness so much as a different mode of existence.<br /> <br /> If one wants to reincarnate, that decision should be respected, but the 1e-2e text has always condemned decisions to the contrary, whether that's remaining as a ghost or escaping the cycle through oblivion. Which is really jarring given A) the reincarnation is arbitrary unless you sell yourself to a god like Ahlat or cough up the right bribes and B) the reincarnation process is corrupt from both bribery and things like Taru-Han's soul collection. The Lumina from the Ink Monkey Daystar write-up were interesting because oh-my-god they were<i> different</i>, a positively portrayed transhuman afterlife that didn't involve becoming some god's furniture or menial servant or something equally degrading. Ghosts were always portrayed as being in the wrong somehow just by being present and not submitting themselves to what Yu-Shan wants. Even when the entire reason the reincarnation cycle is broken is because the gods and the &quot;proper&quot; exalted created the Neverborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T07:29:31-08:00","id":1293744,"title":"","content":"I want Oblivion to be redefined as a condition or state of being (&quot;nonbeing&quot;, rather), as opposed to a force or quasi-entity. It's not an elemental force of destruction or Schrodinger's monster where it has desires or doesn't. It just means &quot;nonexistence&quot;. Something that has been Obliterated is something that has been destroyed.<br /> <br /> Perma-dead gods? Obliterated.<br /> <br /> The Neverborn? NOT Obliterated, and desperately wanting to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Underworld as we remember it isn't coming back, apparently. I think it's all supposed to be a bunch of different, disjointed Underworlds separated by the Underworld Seas.<br /> <br /> So would the never-ending hole still be around?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:43:55-08:00","id":1293775,"title":"","content":"I think oblivion should be a non-capitalized word that describes a state that can be created, and that some among the dead idealize, rather than a cosmological force.<br /> <br /> It kind of gets in the way of Abyssals as purveyors of gothic melodrama if it's a Thing.<br /> <br /> Going by the description of the Underworld in the core, the pit in the centre of Stygia sounds more like a big well, although it might still be a pit into which all of the rivers flow. And that's enough, just a scary feature of the world, not the one unobstructed path to the end of everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T08:48:01-08:00","id":1293778,"title":"","content":"I think it would be interesting for the Mouth of the Void in Stygia to be terrifying not because it represents obliteration, but because none of the non-spectre ghosts have any idea of where it leads. Its a complete unknown, and fear of the unknown is very primal. The Void as a cthonic mystery offers up more plot avenues than infinite nothingness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24948,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","user":"HamSandLich","date":". 03-04-2019, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T09:52:06-08:00","id":1293807,"title":"","content":"Oblivion - emptiness, nothingness<br /> Void - emptiness, nothingness<br /> Abyss - an emptiness so deep that the light does not reveal an end such that it seems to descend forever<br /> <br /> Kaos - the Grecoroman and even Judean concept of emptiness and nothingness of formlessness, before defined forms were created. To the Greeks, Kaos was both a state of pre-existence, a place where things still didn't really exist, and a female Primordial figure who birthed other pre-Titan Primordials like Nyx, the deity of the night, as well as Gaia and Uranus. To the Hebrews, the world was formless chaos of (or merely like) a large body of water (and the sea/ocean has always symbolized godless chaos to the Hebrews) devoid of light and solid forms before God began creating the Earth, starting with light.<br /> <br /> <br /> What might be interesting is a new take on the Underworld where it's actually something of a throwback to an &quot;original Wyld&quot;, if the Wyld were Primordial Chaos thrown into a riotous mess of echoes of Creation by the act of making Creation and imposing direction and juxaposition upon nothingness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 03-04-2019, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T12:11:15-08:00","id":1293848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1293744#post1293744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Underworld as we remember it isn't coming back, apparently. I think it's all supposed to be a bunch of different, disjointed Underworlds separated by the Underworld Seas.<br /> <br /> So would the never-ending hole still be around?</div> </div> </div> </div>But... but... but Stygia! Stygia in all its decadent glory needs to be perched precariously over the giant hole! It just wouldn't be the same without it! <br /> <br /> Also, one of the charms of Single Point, Six-Demon Scabbard Binding refers to Eternal Nova cutting his way out of oblivion, so I will stubbornly believe it's still canon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1293744#post1293744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What might be interesting is a new take on the Underworld where it's actually something of a throwback to an &quot;original Wyld&quot;, if the Wyld were Primordial Chaos thrown into a riotous mess of echoes of Creation by the act of making Creation and imposing direction and juxaposition upon nothingness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember last edition when they said that the Primordials were from the Wyld, people took it as firm canon that they were just a different form of Unshaped, which kind of flattened the distinctive magic of both Primordials and Unshaped. I hope the writers step very lightly around defining cosmological forces like oblivion or the wild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T12:45:50-08:00","id":1293857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slarn!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1293848#post1293848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... but... but Stygia! Stygia in all its decadent glory needs to be perched precariously over the giant hole!</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing is precariously perched over a hole so gigantic that you build around its rim without the possibility of building bridges over it. And who the fuck would build a metropolis on bridges over a gigantic, bottomless pit that leads down into the most horrible place anyone can imagine?<br /> <br /> Like, what would possibly incentivize that behavior? Is it really so horrible if those people are building as close to it as possible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T13:06:55-08:00","id":1293866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1293857#post1293857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing is precariously perched over a hole so gigantic that you build around its rim without the possibility of building bridges over it. And who the fuck would build a metropolis on bridges over a gigantic, bottomless pit that leads down into the most horrible place anyone can imagine?<br /> <br /> Like, what would possibly incentivize that behavior? Is it really so horrible if those people are building as close to it as possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>What would incentivize that behaviour? Deep unconscious urges towards self-annihilation. The whispers of dead gods burrowing into the back of your mind. A love of morbid melodrama, such as ghosts tend to have. Sincere love of the Neverborn. Or just the fact that many ghosts are barely conscious, act purely out of habit, and don't understand how insane living in Stygia is.<br /> <br /> But if those aren't enough, the practical reasons as I understand them are (1) the need to maintain the giant clock atop the hole which keeps the Underworld from falling deeper into the abyss, and which requires massive manpower (ghostpower?) to worship/fuel it. And (2) it's the primary mine for soulfire crystals, which are necessary to make soulsteel. And mining in the labyrinth and forging soulsteel both require a large population.<br /> <br /> It's a setting element I love, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T13:37:52-08:00","id":1293877,"title":"","content":"You never actually mention whether the city is built over the mouth of the hole, as opposed to on the solid ground around it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T13:39:18-08:00","id":1293879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, one of the charms of Single Point, Six-Demon Scabbard Binding refers to Eternal Nova cutting his way out of oblivion, so I will stubbornly believe it's still canon. </div> </div> </div>The fact that someone cut their way out of it already proves its no longer the same as it was in 2E, though? The only thing indestructible enough to survive it in 2E were the exaltation shards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T14:10:14-08:00","id":1293886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1293879#post1293879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that someone cut their way out of it already proves its no longer the same as it was in 2E, though? The only thing indestructible enough to survive it in 2E were the exaltation shards.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. It's definitely better as a thing you can interact with, and potentially overcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T07:50:32-08:00","id":1294052,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think Stygia being built above a hole into the Labyrinth is sufficiently bad mojo and there are spectres who can be negotiated (and presumably traded with) to varying degrees.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T08:55:40-08:00","id":1294076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1294052#post1294052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think Stygia being built above a hole into the Labyrinth is sufficiently bad mojo and there are spectres who can be negotiated (and presumably traded with) to varying degrees.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I agree, but you've gotten me to question whether &quot;the Labyrinth&quot; is even still a thing, in this fractured new version of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Is the Labyrinth one &quot;island&quot; of the Underworld, or a cthonic bridge between all of the &quot;islands&quot; that works as an alternative (potentially more dangerous) way to travel between them than the &quot;seas&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T09:14:23-08:00","id":1294082,"title":"","content":"Indications are that it does from the Nephwrack and Mortwight write-ups, though the particulars could still be very different.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T10:30:25-08:00","id":1294104,"title":"","content":"Contrary to the points listed here (perhaps unfortunately, since I see views of prevailing posters around here as being actually mechanically better for the theme and sanity of the game that's trying to be played) I'm most excited for a theme that's been dipped toe-in-the-water style towards the end of 2nd edition, the utility of Abyssals to the Underworld, but more (at least for me) the possible connection between reconciliation, the Abyssals and the Neverborn.<br /> <br /> I grok that this isn't the direction the devs are planning to with the Abyssals, as the plan is to set the NB almost entirely out of the picture and push the Deathlords as more interesting/diverse patrons (which is cool, a good direction for this Exalt type).<br /> <br /> But, were I to be fully honest about what gets me excited about running / playing, it's playing out a reconciliation narrative between mortals/gods/Primordials. Probably in the context of Primies this doesn't make much sense but to dash preconceptions about vast alien intelligences against the rocks for a moment, the idea that the very instruments of vengeance could be used instead to address a cosmic wound and through the melding of human mind with Primordial Demiuge(s) iiiiis, well, just kind of my bag. Beating swords into tourniquets, on a cosmic scale, sounds very-very cool to me.<br /> <br /> As far as what I'm (actually) looking forward, charm wise, I'd love to see a return of charms that fulfill the function (though unlikely the form, given the mechanical difference tween editions) of The Old Laws. I'd love to see Abyssal charms that celebrate their status as something new and un-conceived in the cosmos.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how that's going to look given that Abyssals source directly from Deathlords now, but I'm eager to find out. Definitely would love to see Abyssal charms that don't have the &quot;must be this much of a dick to use&quot; stipulation attached..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T19:07:43-08:00","id":1294561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1294104#post1294104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contrary to the points listed here (perhaps unfortunately, since I see views of prevailing posters around here as being actually mechanically better for the theme and sanity of the game that's trying to be played) I'm most excited for a theme that's been dipped toe-in-the-water style towards the end of 2nd edition, the utility of Abyssals to the Underworld, but more (at least for me) the possible connection between reconciliation, the Abyssals and the Neverborn.<br /> <br /> I grok that this isn't the direction the devs are planning to with the Abyssals, as the plan is to set the NB almost entirely out of the picture and push the Deathlords as more interesting/diverse patrons (which is cool, a good direction for this Exalt type).<br /> <br /> But, were I to be fully honest about what gets me excited about running / playing, it's playing out a reconciliation narrative between mortals/gods/Primordials. Probably in the context of Primies this doesn't make much sense but to dash preconceptions about vast alien intelligences against the rocks for a moment, the idea that the very instruments of vengeance could be used instead to address a cosmic wound and through the melding of human mind with Primordial Demiuge(s) iiiiis, well, just kind of my bag. Beating swords into tourniquets, on a cosmic scale, sounds very-very cool to me.<br /> <br /> As far as what I'm (actually) looking forward, charm wise, I'd love to see a return of charms that fulfill the function (though unlikely the form, given the mechanical difference tween editions) of The Old Laws. I'd love to see Abyssal charms that celebrate their status as something new and un-conceived in the cosmos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I like the mix cosmic horror and the cosmic wonder of this approach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1294104#post1294104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how that's going to look given that Abyssals source directly from Deathlords now, but I'm eager to find out. Definitely would love to see Abyssal charms that don't have the &quot;must be this much of a dick to use&quot; stipulation attached.</div> </div> </div> </div>YES!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T19:55:45-08:00","id":1294573,"title":"","content":"What I liked about the Neverborn is that despite their vast unknowable alien-ness, their pathos came across as very human. The way the webcomic <i>Chorus of the Neverborn </i>portrayed them was neat,having this weird, sometimes heartwarming, sometimes codependent, sometimes awkward familial relationship with those who could hear the Whispers. Like even when they were being nihilistic douchebags, they felt like big confused cthulhu grandparents. There was a scene where a Nephwrack was having black comedy self-esteem issues due to being unable to harvest organs and the Neverborn were like: &quot;We believe in you Xylor. We belieeeveee....&quot; and as dark as that moment was, was compelling in its own way. The Neverborn as alien, insane patrons who the Abyssals can try and temporarily comfort for their favor would be an interesting one. Since they're not exactly conscious nor sane, you could have parts of them wanting to protect things in Creation that resonate with their memories and have heroic Abyssals mediating between those personalities and the ones that are all KILLMURDERDEATH. Appeasing the hateful parts of the Neverborn so the more sympathetic parts shine through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24948,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","user":"HamSandLich","date":". 03-06-2019, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T08:56:31-07:00","id":1299227,"title":"","content":"Some wishlisting I have for the Abyssals book.<br /> <br /> -1e Entropy based charms come back in force as a way to help distinguish between Solars and Abyssals even at low levels of investment. For example they used to have a charm called Infirmity Inflicting Gesture that stole Strength from their opponent, I'd much rather have that as their counterpart ot Strength Increasing Exerercise than the mechanically identical Corpse Might Surge.<br /> <br /> -One Soulsteel artifact to represent some hideous crime of the First Age. Don't tell, show.<br /> <br /> -An artifact that's created (at least in part) through necrosurgery to show grave robbing hasn't been lost to the Liminal Exalted, maybe even make it an prosthetic like the skeletal hand of an ancient Sidereal thief whose nimble fingers still snarl fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T17:58:27-07:00","id":1299477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1299227#post1299227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-1e Entropy based charms come back in force as a way to help distinguish between Solars and Abyssals even at low levels of investment. For example they used to have a charm called Infirmity Inflicting Gesture that stole Strength from their opponent, I'd much rather have that as their counterpart ot Strength Increasing Exerercise than the mechanically identical Corpse Might Surge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think such a Charm would be out of place, but I also feel as though it's not something they should be confined to in an Edition that is looking to build up more of their own identity independent of being antagonistic towards others.<br /> <br /> {checks back over book}<br /> <br /> Mind, Increasing Strength Exercise is already a Charm that appears primarily concerned with being applied in antagonistic situations, with the benefits of feats just being used at the end, and it does lend a certain cast to Abyssals in the role of glorious undead princes that their athletic prowess and grand stature inflicts a wasting effect upon opponents and competitors that brings them to their knees before the Exalt. Hmm, now that's giving me an image of aiding a feat of strength by way of some kind of decaying effect on an object or structure that renders it functionally lighter for the Abyssal.<br /> <br /> I wonder if such an effect applied upon a character might need to be Instant, in contrast to Increasing Strength Exercise being scene long; I have an inkling that a scene long reduction of another character's damage pools and other applications of Strength might be too powerful, or otherwise throw some of the system off.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T05:31:17-07:00","id":1299563,"title":"","content":"The specifics of how Infirmity Inflicting Gesture is resisted or imposed upon someone is the kind of thing I expect to change between editions.<br /> <br /> Some options off the top of my head-<br /> -You can take cues from how Increasing Strength Exercise was uptated for 3rd edition and allow victims of IIG to pay motes or initiative to shrug off their weakness.<br /> -You can reassess it being a Simple charm that steals most of a character's Strength in one go in favour of a Reflexive charm that drains them one dot at a time.<br /> - You can attach it to a Gambit and worry a lot less about how people are supposed to shrug it off. Makes it much less parallel to ISE and more like a Chi Blocker but it could work depending on what else they have.<br /> -Reducing Strength by 1 point and reducing decisive damage by 1 point are different prospects, just because ISE packages increasing the two together doesn't mean the mirror effect has to if another effect would be more appropriate.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T05:43:05-07:00","id":1299565,"title":"","content":"But super strength is absolutely on-theme for abyssals because vampires stronk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T05:59:16-07:00","id":1299567,"title":"","content":"There's ways to give them super strength without duplicating the Solar charm and putting it in the same place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T07:23:35-07:00","id":1299587,"title":"","content":"Stygia and the Underworld as a whole are the part of Exalted most strongly attached to the &quot;before the World of Darkness&quot; that was going to be the original premise of the line. The part of Stygia and the Labyrinth and the stairs leading down see Wraith and any number of the supplements. The new description of the Sea and storm same as Wraith with byways and passages between the areas being few and far between.<br /> However this really opens up a Indianna Jones type story for Abyssals in the Underworld. All things destroyed can be found in the Underworld and I imagine even artifacts could make it into the Underworld through Shadowlands and the actions of ghosts. <br /> The Abyssals should have charms only useable in the Underworld and possibly tied to limit that affect where and how that charm can be used. For example Restore the lost this charm allows the Abyssal to return Intelligence and Lore motes to a ghost. If an Abyssal is above the halfway point of his limit this charm instead can be used to restore notes to a spectre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T11:59:02-07:00","id":1299676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1299587#post1299587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Abyssals should have charms only useable in the Underworld and possibly tied to limit that affect where and how that charm can be used.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've tried that before. It... wasn't good.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T09:34:50-07:00","id":1299979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1299676#post1299676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've tried that before. It... wasn't good.</div> </div> </div> </div> Spectral was a trash fire but Nightmare-Carving Murmur had potential, though its similarity to the spell The Clay of Warped Dreams raises the question of what the line between Abyssal charms and Necromancy is. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T10:24:50-07:00","id":1299995,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think there's probably room in the Abyssal charmset (especially with the generally-larger charmsets that all splats probably have in 3e) for <i>some</i> effects that work better, or even exclusively, in the Underworld. But they definitely shouldn't be a majority, or even a very large minority, nor concentrated in some Abilities but not others. Every Abyssal concept should be functional in both Creation and the Underworld, I think.<br /> <br /> For Nightmare-Carving Murmur, I kind of like the idea that Abyssals <i>can</i> use it on the Wyld, but <i>only</i> to generate blasted heaths, burning deserts, icy tundras, or deady shoals, and have to actively try to not make them shadowlands. The full reshaping ability of Wyld-Shaping Technique would only be present in the Underworld. Also, though, I like the idea that Nightmare-Carving Murmur is, if not usable literally <i>everywhere</i> in the Underworld, at very least much easier to find a suitable place for it than Wyld-Shaping Technique is in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T16:36:38-07:00","id":1300135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1299979#post1299979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Spectral was a trash fire but Nightmare-Carving Murmur had potential, though its similarity to the spell The Clay of Warped Dreams raises the question of what the line between Abyssal charms and Necromancy is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nightmare-Carving Murmur is fine. There's no problem with having effects that only work in the Underworld because they specifically, inherently only work there - a charm to Wyld Shape the Underworld obviously only works on the Underworld, and that's fine (just like Wyld-Shaping Technique only works in the Wyld, because duh). It's a problem when you have any effect that could conceivably work outside of the Underworld, which gets arbitrarily gated off because &quot;hey stop trying to do cool stuff outside your designated area, dumb Abyssal&quot;, or when you have more than one or two such effects scattered through the charmset (no matter how reasonable the individual effects may be, if 20% of the Abyssal charmset is stuff that only works in the Underworld, it's a bad charmset).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T17:24:46-07:00","id":1300147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1300135#post1300135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a problem when you have any effect that could conceivably work outside of the Underworld, which gets arbitrarily gated off because &quot;hey stop trying to do cool stuff outside your designated area, dumb Abyssal&quot;, or when you have more than one or two such effects scattered through the charmset (no matter how reasonable the individual effects may be, if 20% of the Abyssal charmset is stuff that only works in the Underworld, it's a bad charmset).</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely agree with this. 20% is probably the absolute maximum number of effects in any given Ability that I'd like to see be Underworld-only, and ideally less than that for most of them. And they should absolutely be effects that really <i>do </i>only work in the Underworld, not just stuff that other splats can do in Creation or wherever, and Abyssals, for some reason, can only pull off in the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T20:01:24-07:00","id":1300181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1299587#post1299587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However this really opens up a Indianna Jones type story for Abyssals in the Underworld. All things destroyed can be found in the Underworld and I imagine even artifacts could make it into the Underworld through Shadowlands and the actions of ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm totally with you on this: as heroes who are thematically associated with death, the grave, and things long lost and buried, Abyssals make great Archaeologists and Historians!<br /> <br /> There was an Exalted 3e Actual Play I read a while back where one of the Abyssal NPCs was a chipper tomb-raider trying to uncover the history and stories of long-lost civilizations.<br /> <br /> I personally have been mulling over an Abyssal character concept for a while, a Swordswoman poet who roams the countryside collecting scraps of folklore about an ancient, vanished kingdom...then singing a poem/casting a Necromancy spell that literally brings the dead city-state back to (un)life...not just the citizen ghosts, but the temples, gardens, artifacts, and fortress walls as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12641-aldosalt","name":"AldoSalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12641_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T08:35:29-07:00","id":1300556,"title":"","content":"I'd be... maybe okay... with charms that functioned only in the Underworld, but even better would be charms that had more potency in the underworld, but less potency in Creation (or during daylight, etc).<br /> <br /> Of course, all this hinges heavily on how the Underworld is presented. Most importantly one would have to make the Underworld.. ehh, dynamic? Capable of change? More than just the infected wound of a leftover war.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, this sort of statement then closes off the story possibility of &quot;healing&quot; the underworld and restoring the &quot;natural&quot; cycle of reincarnation. <br /> Admittedly that's not a story I have any interest in, but it is a possible story one could pursue, and my tastes aren't any more deserving of author vindication than anyone else's..<br /> <br /> Okay, rambling caveat aside, one kinda has to answer whether or not the underworld is &quot;worth&quot; saving in their individual stories/campaigns, but the game text itself should, ideally, be able to support both visions.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if the current crop of writers can thread that very tricky needle I'd find a small subset of Underworld only charms, eh, fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T03:26:27-07:00","id":1304137,"title":"","content":"Another place where 3rd edition helps Abyssals immensely.<br /> <br /> In 2nd edition being able to kill people with your Performance, Presence, Medicine etc was kind of shit. While it could be cool, in the grand scheme of things it meant that your ability was being hijacked to give you options to kill people that were often strictly inferior to just picking up a sword.<br /> <br /> Third Edition favours this approach a lot more because these unconventional approaches tend to circmuvent or mitigate the need to build up initiative, either through debilitating gambits or limited effects that determine damage their own way making them tools that can be employed against opponents who refuse to conceed an advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T05:41:09-07:00","id":1304167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1304137#post1304137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third Edition favours this approach a lot more because these unconventional approaches tend to circmuvent or mitigate the need to build up initiative, either through debilitating gambits or limited effects that determine damage their own way making them tools that can be employed against opponents who refuse to conceed an advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does sound like a worthwhile application of this system's plasticity, even if it wouldn't be the sole focus of what they do.<br /> <br /> Yes, I think that putting deadly arts by way of gambits and decisive attacks with their own conditions into those Abilities could cultivate an image of death pervading the Abyssal Exalted, more than them simply being Chosen of Murder so everything they do has to try killing people. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T10:23:56-07:00","id":1304235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1304137#post1304137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2nd edition being able to kill people with your Performance, Presence, Medicine etc was kind of shit. While it could be cool, in the grand scheme of things it meant that your ability was being hijacked to give you options to kill people that were often strictly inferior to just picking up a sword.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting reflection and definitely a point in 3e's favor. As complicated as the initiative system may be (and I've found it not too much hassle after extended use) it more than makes up for it with the ability let offensive powers outside of the normal combat suites shine without overshadowing the utility of more prosaic combat abilities.<br /> <br /> Looking forward to how that'll be expressed when Abyssals starts generating previews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T17:37:10-07:00","id":1304348,"title":"","content":"I think a tight rope to walk for 3e Abyssals will be their Cursed nature and redemption arcs.They're<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> really the only Exalt type where it might be reasonable to regret being exalted.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That's a hard theme to hit while still making them appealing, but I wouldn't want to lose that thematic space.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T17:57:26-07:00","id":1304354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1304235#post1304235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the utility of more prosaic combat abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I've often feared that the prosaic combat Abilities are the harder ones to make more distinct and interesting for Abyssals, while not being so far afield that they don't properly feel like dark mirrors of Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T18:30:52-07:00","id":1304369,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the essence drainers were solid in that regard thematically, but mechanically oh boy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T19:57:47-07:00","id":1304378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1304348#post1304348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're really the only Exalt type where it might be reasonable to regret being exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think for any Exalt type the Wyld Hunt gets sent after, it might be reasonable to regret it. Getting Wyld Hunted sucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T20:24:35-07:00","id":1304383,"title":"","content":"I'm suddenly picturing the path to becoming a Solar as fuelled less by an internal moral shortcoming of Abyssal Exaltation and more as an outgrowth of a kind of inherent romantic streak that might exist in the cross-section between the Essence and the kinds of people who get Chosen, possibly combined a bit with an affectation of melancholic gloom. It's just that the fact that it actually was originally a Solar Exaltation gives that sentiment somewhere to go.<br /> <br /> Something about Abyssals often makes me think of that episode of Blackadder where Shelly, Byron and Coleridge make a very big show over how they're all dying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T20:44:24-07:00","id":1304386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1304378#post1304378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think for any Exalt type the Wyld Hunt gets sent after, it might be reasonable to regret it. Getting Wyld Hunted sucks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah like, there's lots of reasons why being say, a Sidereal is the Worst. For your puissant mind and your determination to set the course of history right youa re rewarded with... An inescapable job. But what I mean is that those things aren't part and parcel with your nature. Abyssals, for me, are partially defined by being cursed. That doesn't mean they all have to be miserable or that their mechanics should discourage you from embracing being an Abyssal. I just think that in terms of their themes, they inhabit it more fully than the next closest contender.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T14:48:29-07:00","id":1304512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1304383#post1304383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm suddenly picturing the path to becoming a Solar as fuelled less by an internal moral shortcoming of Abyssal Exaltation and more as an outgrowth of a kind of inherent romantic streak that might exist in the cross-section between the Essence and the kinds of people who get Chosen, possibly combined a bit with an affectation of melancholic gloom. It's just that the fact that it actually was originally a Solar Exaltation gives that sentiment somewhere to go.<br /> <br /> Something about Abyssals often makes me think of that episode of Blackadder where Shelly, Byron and Coleridge make a very big show over how they're all dying.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since Abyssals don't go insane (at least, more insane than they regularly are) on an episodic basis, i've had an idea for a former Dawn turned Dusk who's actually more in control of himself as a Deathknight than he was as a Solar, and feels that he can do more good as an Abyssal since he noticed he stopped going crazy on a regular basis. Sure, they've got Chivalry of Death in 3e, but it sounds like one of the Paths from VtM where by adhering to a code lets them hold onto their humanity(like how Acts of Villainy were for Infernal Torment), while Solars have very little control over Limit. Solars can get high on their own power and hype to the point of going off the deep end (even without Limit Break), whereas Abyssals(especially former Solars) have that formative moment of weakness(i.e. dying or giving into the Neverborn) that I like to think can keep them grounded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T15:06:44-07:00","id":1304517,"title":"","content":"Third Edition Abyssals will be subject to the Great Curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T10:50:12-07:00","id":1304641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1292632-the-atmosphere-of-abyssal-exalted?p=1304517#post1304517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third Edition Abyssals will be subject to the Great Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, but the way Chivalry of Death is described, it sounds like they'll be able to bleed off Limit by adhering to the code. The same way Infernals could reduce Torment with Acts of Villainy. And how Kindred in VtM could follow one of the Paths to stave off the Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T03:07:17-07:00","id":1410637,"title":"","content":"I think, if you're looking for the inspiration for The Chivalry of Death, look no farther than the literary trope of The Byronic Hero (invented and largely based on idealized perception of himself by Lord George Gordon Byron) and at 18th -century German Romanticism, especially the ideas of Liebestod and Sturm und Drang. As I'm too lazy to explicate on my own, I'll provide links: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byronic_hero\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/44/Byronharlow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byronic_hero\" target=\"_blank\"> Byronic hero - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byronic_hero\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byronic_hero </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Byronichero#:~:text=A%20Byronic%20hero%20is%20a,or%20tragedies%20in%20their%20past.\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.p...0their%20past.</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_Romanticism#:~:text=German%20Romanticism%20was%20the%20dominant,%2C%20aesthetics%2C%20literature%20and%20criticism.\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Caspar_David_Friedrich_-_Mondaufgang_am_Meer_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-Caspar_David_Friedrich_-_Mondaufgang_am_Meer_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_Romanticism#:~:text=German%20Romanticism%20was%20the%20dominant,%2C%20aesthetics%2C%20literature%20and%20criticism.\" target=\"_blank\"> German Romanticism - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_Romanticism#:~:text=German%20Romanticism%20was%20the%20dominant,%2C%20aesthetics%2C%20literature%20and%20criticism.\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_Romanticism#:~:text=German%20Romanticism%20was%20the%20dominant,%2C%20aesthetics%2C%20literature%20and%20criticism. </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jena_Romanticism\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Schlegels.jpg/1280px-Schlegels.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jena_Romanticism\" target=\"_blank\"> Jena Romanticism - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jena_Romanticism\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jena_Romanticism </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sturm_und_Drang\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Andreas_Achenbach_-_Clearing_Up%E2%80%94Coast_of_Sicily_-_Walters_37116.jpg/1280px-Andreas_Achenbach_-_Clearing_Up%E2%80%94Coast_of_Sicily_-_Walters_37116.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sturm_und_Drang\" target=\"_blank\"> Sturm und Drang - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sturm_und_Drang\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sturm_und_Drang </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://blog.blo.org/love-death-or-liebestod#:~:text=Liebestod%20(from%20the%20German%20Liebe,and%20survives%20lovers'%20corporeal%20bodies.\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://blog.blo.org/love-death-or-liebestod#:~:text=Liebestod%20(from%20the%20German%20Liebe,and%20survives%20lovers'%20corporeal%20bodies.\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://blog.blo.org/love-death-or-liebestod#:~:text=Liebestod%20(from%20the%20German%20Liebe,and%20survives%20lovers'%20corporeal%20bodies.\" target=\"_blank\"> http://blog.blo.org/love-death-or-liebestod#:~:text=Liebestod%20(from%20the%20German%20Liebe,and%20survives%20lovers'%20corporeal%20bodies. </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> I believe that from 1st edition, one of the aspects of the Abyssal Exalted was to be grounded in the Byronic Hero. They didn't quite pull it off. It was more Romero bedecked in black roses. The British Romantic poets of the early 19th century make for great Abyssal inspiration, particularly the so-called &quot;Satanic School&quot;: Lord Byron, Percy Shelley, John Keats - I think William Blake is a Sidereal or more likely a Getimian. Coleridge I suppose could represent a world-weary Abyssal addicted to the Guild's heroin. His poetry explores metaphysical aspects of the border of life and death, sure (after all, the Ancient Mariner is won in a dice game by Life-in-Death) but he lacks that savage spirit or romantic evil longing that can turn them into sexy slayers or aesthetes of carnage. Wordsworth is off wandering lonely as a cloud, so let's forget him. Keats wrote delicate poems in which the shadow of time seemed to lay on everything from the petals of lilacs in the morning to the tolling of the church bell at dawn. He also wrote Gothic inspired poem s, La belle dans sans merci, and the vampiric Lamia. He seemed presciently aware of his death at 25 of tuberculosis. Shelley, though wild and anti-Estalishment, was too high hearted and positive that Man would be bettered by knowledge and poetry; Shelley is a revolutionary bipolar Solar while his good friend Lord Byron is a brooding Abyssal aware of his evil deeds and the inevitability of more to come, however much he joys in his friend Shelley;s ideals. There's an inspiration for a couple of characters.<br /> <br /> So, this turned out to be more of a lit lesson and its application to Abyssal role-playing themes than any application of these influences to the thematic design of Abyssal powers and charms, Sorry about that,<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1858-comrade-pointdexter","name":"Comrade Pointdexter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1858_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T21:28:29-08:00","id":1528871,"title":"","content":"It was back in the early 2000's, in my group we were pitching each other different RPGs we owned. One friend talked us into playing 2e Exalted via explaining all the off the wall shit you could get up to by way of describing Invincible Sword Princess. We were figuring out names and, to sweeten the pot and probably show off a bit, he offered to write our character's names in Old Realm; all well and good but we didn't really know what an Old Realm name sounded or spelled like, he waved it off a bit and told us to go with something like Noun Verbing Noun/Adjective. &quot;Just think of something that sounds right.&quot;<br /> When time came to say mine he replied.<br /> &quot;That's an Abyssal name; I don't run Abyssals.&quot;<br /> My fascination began there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}